meta {
  name: 11 Trace — SNAP denial with structured explanation
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/factgraph/{{ruleset_id}}/query
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{api_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "targets": ["/eligible"],
    "inputs": {
      "/grossEarnedIncome": 3500,
      "/unearnedIncome": 0,
      "/dependentCareExpenses": 0,
      "/rent": 0,
      "/realEstateTaxes": 0,
      "/homeownersAssociationFees": 0,
      "/mortgagePayments": 0,
      "/homeownersInsurance": 0,
      "/meetsCategoricalEligibility": false,
      "/childSupportPaid": 0,
      "/isHomeless": false
    },
    "entities": {
      "/members": [
        {
          "id": "applicant",
          "/members/*/isElderly": false,
          "/members/*/isDisabled": false,
          "/members/*/medicalExpenses": 0,
          "/members/*/age": 30,
          "/members/*/isHigherEdStudent": false,
          "/members/*/weeklyWorkHours": 40,
          "/members/*/isWorkStudy": false,
          "/members/*/isParent": false,
          "/members/*/isFullTimeCollegeStudent": false,
          "/members/*/receivesTanf": false,
          "/members/*/isImmigrationEligible": true,
          "/members/*/isPregnant": false,
          "/members/*/isIncapableOfSelfCare": false,
          "/members/*/abawdCountableMonthsUsed": 0,
          "/members/*/cashOnHand": 0,
          "/members/*/bankAccountAssets": 0,
          "/members/*/stockAssets": 0,
          "/members/*/bondAssets": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    "include": ["trace"]
  }
}

docs {
  This scenario walks the structured explanation API.

  Same household as request 06 but with $3,500 of monthly earned income
  — over the gross-income threshold for a single-person household, no
  BBCE, no elderly/disabled members, so the engine resolves /eligible
  to false.

  Setting include: ["trace"] makes the response carry a `traces` map
  keyed by target path. Each entry is a recursive tree showing how
  the target's value was derived:

    - At each `All` that's false, the deciding (first-false) branch is
      called out in the `reason`. The other branches still appear in
      `children` so the caller can see the full picture.
    - At each `Any` that's true, the satisfying branch is called out.
    - Leaf comparisons surface the concrete operand values in `reason`
      — "Gross monthly income (3500) ≤ Gross income limit (1695.2) —
      did not hold."
    - Policy citations from references.json flow through inline on
      facts that have them.

  Arithmetic operators (Multiply, Subtract, etc.) and Switch are
  surfaced as "opaque" — value is present but the walker doesn't
  descend into them. Issue a follow-up query against the intermediate
  fact (e.g. /grossIncomeLimit) to see its breakdown.
}
